<%# Roe lost track of a deploy — usually because Roe was quit or restarted
    while it ran. `target` is "kamal" or "fly". %>
<p>
  Roe was quit or restarted while this deploy was running, so it never
  finished. Nothing was left running in the background.
</p>

<ol>
  <li>Deploy again — it's safe.</li>
  <% if target == "fly" %>
    <li>If that deploy is blocked on a machine lease, this one left it behind. Clear it with <code>fly machine leases clear</code>, then deploy again.</li>
  <% else %>
    <li>If that deploy says the deploy lock is already in place, this one left it behind. Release it with <code>kamal lock release</code>, then deploy again.</li>
  <% end %>
</ol>

<p>
  More detail:
  <a href="/documentation/roe/troubleshoot-deployment" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Troubleshooting → Deployment</a>
</p>
